hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"130","Allahu Akbar, Allahu a'zzu min khalqihi jami'an, Allahu a'zzu mimma akhafu wa ahadhir, a'udhu billahi alladhi la ilaha illa huwa, al-musammasika al-samawati al-sab'i an taqa'a ala al-ardhi illa bi-idhnihi, min sharri 'abdika fulan, wa junudihi wa atba'ihi wa ashya'ihi, min al-jinni wa al-insi, Allahumma kun li jaran min sharrihim, jalla thana'uka wa 'azza jarika, wa tabaraka ismuka, wa la ilaha ghayruka (thalath marrat). Allah is the Greatest, Allah mightier than all His creation, Allah is mightier than what I fear and dread. I seek refuge in Allah, there is no god but He, the One Who holds the seven heavens from falling upon the earth except by His permission, from the evil of Your servant so-and-so, and his soldiers, followers, and supporters, from among the jinn and mankind. O Allah, be my protector from their evil. Glorified are Your praises, and honored is Your protection, and blessed is Your name, and there is no god but You (three times)."
"131","Allāhumma munzila al-kitābi, sarīʿa al-ḥisābi, ihziim al-aḥzāba, Allāhumma ihziimhum wa zalzilhum.. O Sender of the Book, O Swift in reckoning, defeat the confederates. O God, defeat them and shake them."
